<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA ISSUES $ 17 MLN DEPOSIT GUARANTEE T-NOTES.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA ISSUES $ 17 MLN DEPOSIT GUARANTEE T-NOTES.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry placed $16.954 million of three-year floater coupon T-notes to cover payments to depositors in banks that the central bank seeks to close down, the Bulgarian National BANK (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The paper was placed with the Bulgarian Post Bank, which in mid-July began to pay foreign currency depositors of ailing banks slated for bankruptcy.</p>
<p>The paper bears a semi-annual coupon set at two points over a six-month LIBOR, the BNB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The BNB has opened bankruptcy procedures through the courts against five banks since May.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	BG 2032796117</p>
<p> Par value	   $16.954 mln</p>
<p> Issue date	  September 12, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date     September 9, 1999</p>
<p> Coupon		LIBOR + 2 points</p>
<p>-- Dessislava Popova, Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
</text>
